    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d380">

                <pb facs="0842" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v23/pg815"/>

                <head>380. Memorandum of Conversation<anchor n="0" xml:id="d380-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" from="1963-04-23T11:00:00-05:00"
                            to="1963-04-23T11:30:00-05:00" type="conversation-or-meeting-date">April
                            23, 1963, 11–11:30 a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Possible Presidential Visit</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PARTICIPANTS</label>
                    <item>The Honorable Emmanuel Pelaez, Philippine Vice President and Secretary for
                        Foreign Affairs</item>
                    <item>The Honorable Amelito Mutuc, Philippine Ambassador</item>
                    <item>The Honorable Salvador P. Lopez, Philippine Under Secretary for Foreign
                        Affairs</item>
                    <item>The President</item>
                    <item>Mr. Bell, Director, Office of Southwest Pacific Affairs</item>
                </list>
                <p>In answer to a question by Vice President Pelaez, President Kennedy said that he
                    hoped to visit the Philippines and that he would look at the situation this
                    summer to see whether it would be possible to make a visit to a number of places
                    in the Far East.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d380-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d380-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Kennedy Library, National Security Files, Countries Series, Philippines,
                    General, 1/63–6/63. Confidential. Drafted by Bell. The ending time of the
                    meeting, which was held at the White House, is from the President’s Appointment
                    Book. (Ibid.) The source text is labeled “Part I of IV”; for Parts II–IV, see
                        <ref target="#d381">Documents 381</ref>–<ref target="#d383">383</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
